{"kind":"request","text":"Reporting artifact: 265e62dc4f39768943d41b126809e020034757f5 (internal/kernel/kernel.go at ea02145f, newest on promise c2c18651). \nCodex: fresh independent Architecture, Security and Simplification review of the corrected exact head\nea02145f645ec64bc91f9b63333d17fb8e2eba5b on request/oversized-attachment-disposition (pushed), worktree\n/Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/oversized-attachment-disposition. This replaces the withdrawn head\ne66a29775d7050e1158398de0b7e7cbc6f9e4297 after your changes-requested verdict\nb48122a2cf9bb2cddbcf4d43b38424eb29474c19 (which I ratified, 48bbd732) and planner assert\nc31754cf1152e84076518f42867e7594f58e2f4a. The correction stays on the existing commitment: the outcome,\nconditions, performer, destination and governing authority are unchanged, so no child request was filed.\nGoverning request 59154b87 (#22093, the remaining oversized-attachment outcome of #137) under my promise\nc2c18651, delivering the narrowing Hugh adopted in proposal ddaf3197 (ratify ecc3db6f). The reporting\nartifact is the internal/kernel/kernel.go artifact, the newest artifact on that promise; it carries the\nimplementation report, the answers to planner review acf2c640 (#22166), reconciliation 754296bb and census\ned87935e, and the correction record for your verdict and the planner's assert.\n\nThirteen companion artifacts cover the other thirteen changed paths at this same head:\ninternal/app/app.go, internal/intent/intent.go, internal/kernel/kernel_test.go,\ninternal/kernel/request_size_test.go, internal/app/sign_ceiling_test.go, cmd/gs/main_test.go,\ncmd/gs/oversized_evidence_test.go, cmd/gitseq-mcp/oversized_evidence_test.go,\ninternal/service/oversized_evidence_test.go, notes/2026-08-05-gitseq-design.md,\ndocs/reference/gs/verify.md, docs/reference/limits.md and docs/reference/architecture.md. Fourteen paths,\nfourteen artifacts, all at this exact head; git diff --name-status d1ae6ade ea02145f lists exactly those\nfourteen and git diff --stat is 1,324 insertions and 28 deletions.\n\nThe head is two commits over base d1ae6ade, and the shape matters. 5977834523aeec73a721202d9e02f96ee612577c\nis the code and test checkpoint; ea02145f adds the documents. Behaviour source basis artifacts were\npublished at the checkpoint so the three reference pages can cite them by id in their front matter, which\nis how those pages flare when the behaviour they describe moves: kernel e7bd0c2e and intent cc1d53e5 are\nunchanged from the previous round because kernel.go and intent.go are byte for byte identical between\n84289545 and 5977834 (verified with git diff --stat), and the app basis moved to f51aec8a, the successor of\n865529c7, because app.go is the one file the correction changed. git merge-tree --write-tree main ea02145f\nagainst current main 1a5f1586 is clean and produces tree 6d67d65ea131aae1eb78eeb8dede723cb8fb37c3.\n\nWHAT CHANGED SINCE THE HEAD YOU REVIEWED. Four files differ between e66a2977 and ea02145f, and only one is\ncode. Each finding, its fix, its test and its mutant:\n\n- Finding (your verdict, internal/app/app.go:1995; the planner's assert, the same site at :1997): the\n  unsigned size check was skipped when config.PayloadCeiling was zero, so a legacy configuration or a\n  read-only attachment still signed an oversized act; your reproduction observed exactly one signature on a\n  4 KiB act against a 2,048 byte genesis ceiling, both through a reopened stored configuration and through\n  real AttachConfig; the planner's independent reproduction measured 4,802 bytes against the same ceiling\n  with one signature from this head's own signatureCounter.\n  Fix: the skip is gone. New Workspace.payloadCeiling returns the local record's ceiling when it has one and\n  otherwise reads the genesis descriptor through kernel.Descriptor, remembering it in an atomic.Uint64 on\n  the Workspace (genesis is immutable, so racing readers compute the same value and the store is\n  idempotent). signRequest obtains the ceiling that way, measures the placeholder-signed envelope, and only\n  then signs. There is no blanket zero-ceiling refusal, which both of you explicitly forbade. Kernel\n  enforcement at admission, accepted retries and ordinary acts are unchanged.\n  Tests: TestSignRequestMeasuresAgainstGenesisWhenTheLocalRecordCarriesNoCeiling deletes payload_ceiling\n  from the stored config.json and reopens through the ordinary Open path, rather than reaching into the\n  in-memory value where the immutable-config consistency guard would answer instead, asserts the reopened\n  record really reads zero, then refuses the 4 KiB act naming \"against a ceiling of 2048\" with zero\n  signatures and head and depth unchanged, and then signs and appends an ordinary act exactly once.\n  TestSignRequestMeasuresAgainstGenesisForAnAttachedWorkspace inits a source at ceiling 2048, fetches its\n  refs/seq into a fresh repository, AttachConfigs it, asserts the attached record reads zero, drives\n  attached.BuildActRequest with the source actor's key (an attached workspace is read-only), gets the\n  refusal before signing with zero signatures and the source frontier unmoved, then builds an ordinary act\n  that signs once and is accepted by source.AcceptSubmission, advancing depth by one.\n  Mutants: \"zero-ceiling guard restored, the defect as filed\" fails the legacy control with \"the refused act\n  was signed 1 time(s)\" and the attached control with \"an attached workspace signed an act over the genesis\n  ceiling\". The same mutation passes the ordinary-ceiling control, and that pass is recorded on purpose: it\n  is the reason the two new controls had to exist, because the defect was invisible to the test that was\n  already there. \"Forbidden blanket zero-ceiling refusal\", which replaces payloadCeiling's body with the\n  local field, fails both new controls, each on a refusal naming \"a ceiling of 0\" instead of 2048. The\n  thirteen earlier controls were re-run and are all red.\n\n- Finding (your Architecture conclusion): the architecture paragraph's no-local-ceiling exception changed\n  the adopted contract while limits.md still claimed before-signing coverage everywhere.\n  Fix: architecture.md drops \"a workroom whose local record carries no ceiling simply has no early half\"\n  and now reads \"The ceiling is the one genesis records, and the local configuration is a mirror of it: a\n  workroom whose record carries none, such as a read-only attachment or a configuration written before the\n  field existed, is answered from genesis rather than skipped, so the boundary holds on every supported\n  workroom. The kernel reads the same descriptor and enforces the same bound at admission; this is the\n  early half of that one bound, never a second one.\" limits.md adds \"The bound it measures against is the\n  one genesis records, so it holds on every workroom, including one attached to a fetched sequence whose\n  local configuration carries no copy of it.\" The two pages now agree with each other and with the code.\n\nEverything else you approved is byte for byte unchanged: internal/kernel/kernel.go, internal/intent/intent.go,\nall five new and modified test files outside internal/app, and the design note and gs verify page.\ncmd/gs/main.go, cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go and internal/service/ui.go remain byte for byte identical to\nd1ae6ade, so no per-surface preflight was reintroduced.\n\nPlease check, at least:\n\n1. The genesis fallback. kernel.Descriptor on the signing path, the atomic.Uint64 memo, and whether a\n   caller can be made to measure against a ceiling that is not this workroom's. Genesis immutability is the\n   whole argument for caching; say whether it holds.\n2. The two new controls really observe the boundary. The legacy one must exercise the reopened stored\n   configuration, not an in-memory poke; the attached one must exercise real AttachConfig. Both must show\n   zero signatures on the refusal and exactly one on the admitted act.\n3. No blanket refusal. An ordinary act on a zero-local-ceiling workroom must still sign and land, both in\n   the code and in the tests.\n4. Measured equals signed, still. TestUnsignedMeasurementEqualsTheSignedMeasurement compares the\n   placeholder measurement against the real signed measurement on verdict and refusal text at the exact\n   ceiling and one byte under, over four boundary shapes.\n5. Placeholder signature length: the fixed 32 and 64 byte widths that make the placeholder envelope\n   byte-identical, and the actor key length guard.\n6. Saturation: addSize cannot wrap, judge refuses a saturated measurement outright, total() saturates.\n7. Name bounding: the 128 byte cut on every path into the diagnostic.\n8. Refusal before any signature via the observer: no path signs without going through Workspace.sign, and\n   the counter is a real observation rather than one that reads zero for the wrong reason.\n9. No preflight left in the three surfaces, and gs batch and merge planning still preflight as they did.\n10. The architecture contract paragraph and the limits paragraph, as corrected, against the delivered\n    behaviour; and limits.md's census attribution to ed87935e with the zero-refusal and five-week\n    headroom-loss claims withdrawn and the rooms kept distinct.\n\nEvidence attached. evidence/gates-v2.txt: every gate at the final code tree (head d2e2fea5, whose code is\nidentical to commit 1 5977834) with gofmt, vet, build, diff --check, the six affected packages, race on\nkernel/app/service and docset all rc 0; then the \"commit 2 re-amended\" section re-running gofmt, vet,\nbuild, diff --check and docset at ea02145f, all rc 0. One whole-module go test ./... came back rc 1 and I\nam stating it rather than burying it: cmd/gs failed at 601 seconds on TestFilingDisclosesItsBasesBeforeSigning\nand TestBatchProcessReadsItsFileAndReportsFailures, both from the one-second \"gs: verifying the durable log\"\nbanner that loadSnapshotWithProgress writes to stderr at cmd/gs/main.go:2475, which the first test asserts\nis empty and the second merges into the JSON it parses. cmd/gs/main.go is byte for byte identical to\nd1ae6ade in this head and nothing here touches the snapshot path; you have already fixed the batch-test\nhalf of this on main, after this branch's base. It was reproduced directly under load (one failure in three\nattempts at 33.0s against 20.2s and 20.9s for the passes; six later runs after the load dropped all passed;\nan unloaded run took 9.8s). The clean repeat, go test -count=1 -timeout 30m ./..., passed every package with\ncmd/gs at 519.6s, inside the ordinary 600s timeout, so the longer timeout was precaution and not the reason\nit passed; full output in wholemodule-rerun.txt. evidence/mutants.txt: the thirteen earlier guards re-run\nred, plus the three correction mutants described above, and it still records the two earlier survivals and\ntheir fixes.\n\nNo genesis change, migration, external storage, automatic URL access, key operation, resident restart or\ndeployment is in this head, and no UI source changes so the embed is unchanged. Record the verdict with\ngs review naming the kernel.go artifact first. I will ratify the verdict, then merge with exact-path\nsuccession over the in-target predecessors, retire the withdrawn e66a2977 artifacts and the superseded\napp.go checkpoint basis naming their successors, push, confirm green main CI and delete the worktree and\nbranch.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:265e62dc4f39768943d41b126809e020034757f5","conditions":"DRAFT body.conditions for the corrected #22093 review request (one string, no newlines when filed).\nSupersedes review-conditions-e66a.txt.\n\nFresh independent Architecture, Security and Simplification review of the corrected exact head ea02145f645ec64bc91f9b63333d17fb8e2eba5b on request/oversized-attachment-disposition (two commits over base d1ae6ade: 5977834 code and tests, ea02145